From 85366eec0f6ec4cf81a6044b09aad258eace92c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Asay <aasay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:26:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Network mode ns:<path>: join an existing network
 namespace

Accept Podman's --network ns:<absolute path> (for example a namespace
made with ip netns add at /run/netns/<name>). The container joins that
namespace as it is: no bridge, veth, address, published ports or
extra networks, and teardown never changes anything in it. It keeps
its own hostname, /etc/hosts and resolv.conf, so --hostname, --dns and
--add-host apply. docker exec works as for any container.

The daemon validates the path is absolute and refuses port publishing,
a MAC address and links; it passes the path to the agent as the new
netns_path net option. The agent opens it, checks it is a network
namespace (NS_GET_NSTYPE) and uses it like --network container:.
